WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.070
When a glacier melts back,
it leaves bare ground behind:

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.340
rock and gravel, and no soil at all.

3
00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:09.370
No one plants a thing.

4
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:14.580
Yet in one illustrative survey, plants
that were tiny after 10 years stood as

5
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.270
tall trees after 200.

6
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:22.980
So how can bare rock turn into forest,
without anyone planting a single tree?

7
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.800
In this mission, you'll
see what succession is,

8
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:29.100
and meet the first species
to arrive on bare rock,

9
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.710
tough enough to survive
drought, heat and cold.

10
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.830
Then you'll see where the sequence ends: a
stable community that lasts until something

11
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.150
disturbs it.

12
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.720
Your mission: explain how bare rock can
become forest with no one planting a single

13
00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:45.320
tree.
